It reads the Radio France Open API (https://developers.radiofrance.fr) with
the personal key of each user. This integration is unofficial: it is not
affiliated with nor endorsed by Radio France. Radio France and the names of
its stations (France Inter, franceinfo, France Culture, France Musique, FIP,
Mouv', ICI) belong to Radio France. No logo or brand mark of Radio France is
used: the cover is a generic illustration.

The data shown by the integration is provided by the Radio France Open API
("données fournies par l'Open API Radio France") and is subject to its terms
of use: it is not stored, not modified and not used commercially.

The queries (brands, live, grid) and the shape of the answers were taken from
the official documentation of the Open API and from projects that use it, read
only, no code copied:
  - the Radio France Open API workshop
    (https://github.com/glecoq-rf/openapi-workshop, ISC);
  - the Home Assistant custom integration radio-france-home-assistant
    (https://github.com/kamaradclimber/radio-france-home-assistant, Apache
    License 2.0);
  - whats-on-fip (https://github.com/dixneuf19/whats-on-fip).
The fake API of the tests (test/helpers/fake-openapi.js) answers with those
shapes and with made-up programs only: no data of Radio France is stored in
this repository.
